# Standalone selftest binaries (rustc --edition 2021 --test <x>_selftest.rs -o …).
# ~7.5 MB each and rebuilt on demand — they are output, not source.
/t?.exe
/tt_*.exe
# The packaged game archive and its pristine copy ARE in this repository (the build
# embeds the first, the asset tools rebuild from the second). The scratch copies the
# asset tools drop next to them are not.
hero3_fixed.zip.*
# ★ The same rule for ANY game archive under dist/: carrier download packages (the
# `[KT]…[01.00.08].zip` KT build rode into ffa16e1 by mistake and was untracked on
# 2026-09-20 — it is still in history) and bare jars are licensed content too. dist/ is
# for the signed APK (ignored above via *.apk) and its README, nothing else.
dist/*.zip
dist/*.jar
# ★ Signing keys. They are configured from OUTSIDE the repo (env, or
# %USERPROFILE%\.gradle\gradle.properties) precisely so none of this can ever be
# committed — these patterns are the second line of defence. A leaked release key
# lets anyone ship an "update" to installed copies.
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties
signing.properties

android_app/asset_backup/*
!android_app/asset_backup/hero3_fixed.zip.orig
map_gallery/

# ★ Claude Code's git worktrees. NEVER tracked (2026-09-13).
#
# `881857b` swept these in with a `git add -A` and they have been noise ever since:
# they are gitlinks (mode 160000) with **no `.gitmodules`**, so git records a commit
# SHA it has no URL for — a fresh `clone` gets an EMPTY directory there, and every
# branch a worktree advances (e.g. `vanilla` on a release) leaves the main checkout
# permanently "modified". Untracking costs nothing: the worktrees keep working, and
# `git worktree list` is where they are actually registered.
.claude/worktrees/

# 129차: a scratch copy of the shipped binary.mod (md5 6a352944…, identical to tools_re/_binary.mod) — local tooling only
/_scratch_binary.mod
